course: dictionary
lesson: 14974
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Render is a formal word, so you will meet it in stories and exams. It has several meanings, so the words around it tell you which one is right. Look at the context first.
explain: «The heavy snow rendered the road unusable.» Here render means made, so the snow made the road impossible to use. Try the simple meaning in the sentence: the snow made the road useless. It fits, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «The nurse rendered first aid to the boy who fell.» Here render means gave, so the nurse gave help. In «The translator rendered the poem into English», render means changed into another language. Same word, different job, so always check the sentence.
explain: Computers and builders use render too. A computer renders a picture or video by building it from data. A builder renders a wall by covering it with a layer of cement. Ask yourself what is being rendered, and the meaning becomes clear.
fact: Render can mean to cause something to be in a certain state, as in «rendered helpless».
fact: Render can mean to give help or a service, as in «render a service».
fact: Render can mean to show, perform or translate something in a certain way.
fact: In computing, «render» means to make a picture or video by computer.
fact: In building, «render» means to cover a wall with a layer of plaster or cement.
exercise: «The storm rendered the road unusable.» What does rendered mean here? | Washed clean | Painted | *Made it become, so it was impossible to use | Looked at carefully
exercise: «The nurse rendered first aid to the boy who fell.» What did the nurse do? | *Gave help | Ran away from the boy | Took a photo of the boy | Sold the first aid kit
exercise: Ella watches a 3D film being made. The computer is rendering the pictures. What is it doing? | Showing a cartoon on the TV | Covering the screen with paint | *Building the finished pictures from data | Drawing a map by hand
test: «The builder rendered the outside wall with cement.» What is the builder doing? | Knocking the wall down | Washing the wall clean | *Covering the wall with a layer of cement | Painting the wall with a brush
test: «The translator rendered the poem into English.» What does rendered mean here? | Tore up | Read silently | Memorised | *Turned into
exam: Which sentence uses render to mean give help? | The computer rendered the 3D film. | The snow rendered the road unusable. | *The doctor rendered help to the injured skier. | The builder rendered the wall with cement.
